ity is also unreviewed.\", \"severity\": \"medium\"},\n    {\"claim_id\": \"EXP-049-C1\", \"issue\": \"The ±0.0036 is a std over only 3 folds with 1 repeat, and fold splitting (duplicates, grouping, stratification) is undocumented. Duplicate leakage could inflate high-capacity models such as extra_trees.\", \"severity\": \"high\"},\n    {\"claim_id\": \"EXP-049-C1\", \"issue\": \"The ranking compares untuned default configurations ('baseline'), so 'strongest algorithm family' is not established. It reflects only this default-parameter comparison.\", \"severity\": \"medium\"},\n    {\"claim_id\": \"EXP-049-C1\", \"issue\": \"The claim is worded as a recommendation and correctly notes the unseen holdout, but the bundle's limitations are empty and leave out the validation risks above. It should not be read as cleared for promotion.\", \"severity\": \"low\"}\n  ],\n  \"next_experiment\": {\n    \"title\": \"Duplicate-aware repeated CV re-check of extra_trees vs lightgbm on the ratios feature set\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"The extra_trees advantage over lightgbm (mean ROC-AUC gap of about 0.018 in EXP-049) is not an artifact of duplicate-row leakage or of the 3-fold/1-repeat split, and it persists under group-aware repeated CV with feature generation fitted inside each training fold.\",\n    \"success_gate\": \"On training data only, with identical duplicate-grouped, stratified folds (5 folds × 3 repeats, fixed seeds, feature generation fit inside each training fold), extra_trees beats lightgbm in at least 80% of paired folds with a mean paired ROC-AUC difference ≥ 0.01. Its mean minus 0.25×std score must also remain the highest of the two models. If the paired difference falls below 0.01 or the sign flips in more than 20% of paired folds, the 'extra_trees leader' claim is falsified or downgraded to a tie. Duplicate-row counts and the fold construction are reported either way.\",\n    \"why_smallest\": \"It re-runs only the top two models, once, on the same feature stage 